# Intent: Servo stepping runs in its own task every 20 ms (vTaskDelayUntil, priority above the screen loop, 3 KB stack) instead of in the screen loop, whose period was its delay plus its work (25 to 40 ms with jitter, so the head animation took 26 to 43 steps a second instead of 50). The limiter status reports what is applied: the angle and speed the servo layer last handed to the limiter and got back, with the scale and speed percent used. Bench: self.bench.servo_rate also answers the inter-call time of the servo update (min, median, p95, max) and the stack margin of the servo task. Host test: state free exactly when scale, speed and dance step are full, over every combination of the limiter's inputs.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/hal.cpp, stackchan/motion/servo.cpp and servo.h (M5Stack base, MIT); firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.bench.servo_rate during a yaw move answers steps_per_s near 50 and an interval median of 20 ms with p95 under 30; servo_task_stack_min shows at least 600 bytes of margin; self.motion.status answers an applied block that matches the scale it reports.
# Kconfig: none

